# Cursor Rules Index

## Overview
This is the central index of all Cursor rules. Each rule is documented with its purpose and when it applies.

## Core Rules (Always Applied)

### [general.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/general.mdc)
Core coding principles including file structure, SOLID principles, error handling, and general best practices.
- **Applies to**: All files (`**/*`)
- **Always applied**: Yes

### [security.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/security.mdc)
Security best practices for authentication, authorization, secrets management, and data protection.
- **Applies to**: TypeScript/TSX files (`**/*.{ts,tsx}`)
- **Always applied**: Yes

### [logging.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/logging.mdc)
Structured logging standards with data redaction and context propagation.
- **Applies to**: TypeScript/TSX files (`**/*.{ts,tsx}`)
- **Always applied**: Yes

### [mcp.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/mcp.mdc)
MCP server priority rules and feature validation guidelines, particularly for Tilt integration.
- **Applies to**: All files (`**/*`)
- **Always applied**: Yes

## Testing Rules

### [tests.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/tests.mdc)
Comprehensive testing protocol for unit, integration, and security tests with mandatory coverage requirements.
- **Applies to**: TypeScript and test files (`**/*.{ts,tsx,spec.ts,e2e.ts}`)
- **Always applied**: Yes

### [sonarqube-mcp-testing.mdc](.cursor/rules/specialized/sonarqube-mcp-testing.mdc)
SonarQube integration with testing workflow via MCP server.
- **Applies to**: All files
- **Always applied**: No

### [sonarqube-scan-relationship-rule.mdc](.cursor/rules/specialized/sonarqube-scan-relationship-rule.mdc)
Git-to-SonarQube scan relationships and access patterns for PRs, branches, and commits.
- **Applies to**: TypeScript/TSX files (`**/*.{ts,tsx}`)
- **Always applied**: No

