## Rule Dependencies

### Security and Logging
- [security.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/security.mdc) ↔ [logging.mdc](.cursor/rules/core/logging.mdc)
- Both handle data redaction and sensitive information

### API Design
- [api-design.mdc](.cursor/rules/api/api-design.mdc) ↔ [grpc-patterns.mdc](.cursor/rules/api/grpc-patterns.mdc)
- Both define API communication patterns

### Performance
- [performance.mdc](.cursor/rules/performance/performance.mdc) ↔ [token-optimization.mdc](.cursor/rules/performance/token-optimization.mdc) ↔ [database.mdc](.cursor/rules/data/database.mdc) ↔ [caching.mdc](.cursor/rules/data/caching.mdc)
- All related to performance optimization

## Usage

Rules are automatically applied based on their `alwaysApply` setting and `globs` patterns. Rules with `alwaysApply: true` are always active. Rules with `alwaysApply: false` are applied when their file patterns match.

## Contributing

When adding new rules:
1. Add proper frontmatter with description, globs, and alwaysApply
2. Include integration section linking to related rules
3. Update this index
4. Follow the rule structure template in the plan
